            {
                "entry_id": "aaa6b44a-cbc4-3dc4-aad1-6dee32fab09b",
                "word": "cavendish",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0ef6df29-9cd0-34d8-8d56-4171276afa94",
                        "entry_id": "aaa6b44a-cbc4-3dc4-aad1-6dee32fab09b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Leaf tobacco softened, sweetened, and pressed into plugs or cakes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4b67aab-6b37-44c5-a74f-88530cc0a1e7",
                                "sense_id": "0ef6df29-9cd0-34d8-8d56-4171276afa94",
                                "text": "\"But the managers seem inclined to cut their cavendish very fine just at present,\" she said."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6f82e62-5e09-4db0-8ea9-075f9deacde0",
                                "sense_id": "0ef6df29-9cd0-34d8-8d56-4171276afa94",
                                "text": "No man less; only he (not Vieuxbois, but his younger brother) has found a wide-awake cooler than an iron kettle, and travels by rail when he is at home; and when he was in the Crimea, rode a shaggy pony, and smoked cavendish all through the battle of Inkermann.\" \""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a71e75cf-f5db-416a-8979-9b7a44f6b488",
                                "sense_id": "0ef6df29-9cd0-34d8-8d56-4171276afa94",
                                "text": "Then burn equal parts of cavendish tobacco and old shoeleather in an iron vessel till charred."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40a98f68-3cf4-428b-b7b9-6d9651568464",
                                "sense_id": "0ef6df29-9cd0-34d8-8d56-4171276afa94",
                                "text": "It was always an augury of foul weather in Livingstone's temper when, instead of the decent evening cigar, he smoked the short black brule-gueule, loaded to the muzzle with cavendish."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f3a4a9b-3a9c-4869-ae9e-b47e4ff8a405",
                                "sense_id": "0ef6df29-9cd0-34d8-8d56-4171276afa94",
                                "text": "Come, I'll trate ye to a taste o' me cavendish, which is better than growlin' in yer hammock at the muskaities, poor things, as don't know no better.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
